Subject: [PATCH 0/2] Flush HBM cache via vendor SMC before ACPI hotplug _EJ0

This series adds an ACPI hotplug pre_eject callback and uses it to
notify HiSilicon firmware to flush cache associated with HBM memory
after the memory is removed but before the device is powered down.

Patch 1 adds the pre_eject callback to struct acpi_hotplug_profile
and invokes it from acpi_scan_hot_remove() between acpi_bus_trim()
(which runs .detach -> remove_memory) and acpi_evaluate_lck()/_EJ0
(which powers down the device).

Patch 2 registers the callback in the HiSilicon hbmdev driver and
broadcasts a vendor SMC (HISI_HBMDEV_CACHE_FLUSH_SMC, FID 0x83009000)
to all CPUs via on_each_cpu(), so firmware can perform per-CPU cleanup
such as TLB/cache invalidation against the post-offline state.

Both patches are checkpatch clean (--strict --no-tree) and the kernel
builds without warnings.

Chen Jun (2):
  ACPI: hotplug: add pre_eject callback before device power-down
  soc: hisilicon: hbmdev: flush cache via SMC in pre_eject callback

